<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ukraine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ukrainian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ukraine is a country in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> whose fertile steppe lands have been contested by many powers. Much of it formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, where the Khmelnytsky uprising of 1648 began the loss of eastern territories to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in Ukraine, and its grain lands later became central to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>'s agricultural economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ukraine.jpg" alt="Ukraine" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Ukraine · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukraine.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
